delivery._inject supplies only role=user. Actual installed Hermes inject_plugin_message with mock TUI host rejects keyless injection but accepts explicit session_key. Require verified runtime target key, explicit operator consent and exact profile/session identity; never latest/keyless fallback. Targeting alone cannot repair process-global identity (separate bug). Test idle/busy/ended/unknown/missing-consent targets and preserve mail on refusal. First-turn pre_llm currently skips inbox based on incorrect session-start-drain assumption; registration only registers/joins rooms. Include first-turn queued-mail acceptance, do not claim synchronous delivery based on background fallback.

## Evidence and scope
Isolated mocked probes against installed ~/.hermes/plugins/c2c; seven Python files match c2c data/hermes-plugin. Reproduced by parent via PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 ~/.hermes/cache/scratch/c2c-session-probe.py; results sibling c2c-session-probe-results.json. No live mail, services or configuration touched. Preserve/rehome regression fixture into repo tests before scratch expires. These are isolated reproductions, not observed production disclosure/loss. Coordinate with I016 and B371; separate from frozen b8 B369/B370 relay candidate. No compilation on xsm; use buildboxes for required build gates.


Execution lane and decision (2026-10-22): Decision: shared runtime lane B372→B373→B374→B375. Explicit verified session keys and required operator consent; never infer the latest conversation. Preserve mail for unsupported/ended/unknown targets and process first-turn mail. No automatic gateway opt-in or unrelated session restart.